                     /note="stem-loop V"
                     /function="Stem-loop V binds single polypyrimidine
                     tract-binding protein (PTB) in a unique orientation. PTB
                     RNA-binding domains (RBDs) 1 and 2 interact with the basal
                     part of Domain V, and RBDs3 and 4 binding the putatively
                     single-stranded linkers flanking Domain V. This stimulates
                     IRES activity by inducing eukaryotic translation initiation
                     factor 4 gammaprotein (eIF4G) to bind in the optimal
                     position and orientation to promote internal ribosome
                     entry."
