     proprotein      746..3385
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="precursor polypeptide P1"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:Amino acid sequence analysis
                     cleavage products of the polyprotein.[6264310]"
                     /note="Precursor of structural proteins. 3CDpro cleaves the
                     P1 precursor polypeptide, giving rise to proteins VP0, VP3
                     and VP1."
     proprotein      746..1765
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="capsid protein VP0"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:[6264310]"
                     /note="Precursor of VP4 and VP2 capsid proteins. Cleavage
                     of VP0 into capsid proteins VP4 and VP2 occurs during
                     maturation of the virion."
     mat_peptide     746..949
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="capsid protein VP4"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:x-ray crystallographic methods"
                     /note="Poliovirus capsid is formed from 60 copies of 4 coat
                     protein subunits (VP1, VP2, VP3 and VP4). VP1, VP2 and VP3
                     are the major capsid proteins forming the icosahedral
                     capsid shell (T=3), with a diameter of approximately 300
                     Angstroms. Each of them contains a 'core' consisting of an
                     eight-stranded antiparallel beta barrel with two flanking
                     helices. The capsid protects the viral genome from the
                     environment, and facilitates delivery to appropriate target
                     cells (by binding to the specific poliovirus receptor,
                     PVR). As infection begins, viral RNA must be freed from the
                     capsid during the 'uncoating' process and penetrate the
                     cell. VP4 protein lies on the inner surface of the protein
                     shell formed by VP1, VP2 and VP3. Externalization of VP4
                     (together with N terminus of VP1 and shifts of the capsid
                     beta barrels) initiates irreversible conformational change
                     to the 135S particles ('A' particles) cell entry
                     intermediate. It seems that Poliovirus enters different
                     cells by different mechanisms, and point to a role for
                     virus-induced intracellular signals in the process. PVR
                     mediates virus attachment to target cells, initiates the
                     uncoating process and inducts intracellular signals for
                     virus entry."
                     /protein_id="NP_740468.1"
     mat_peptide     950..1765
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="capsid protein VP2"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:x-ray crystallographic
                     methods[2994218]"
                     /note="See the comment for coat protein VP4."
                     /protein_id="NP_740469.1"
     mat_peptide     1766..2479
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="capsid protein VP3"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:x-ray crystallographic methods[
                     2994218]"
                     /note="See the comment for coat protein VP4."
                     /protein_id="NP_740470.1"
     mat_peptide     2480..3385
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="capsid protein VP1"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE: x-ray crystallographic
                     methods[2994218]"
                     /note="See the comment for coat protein VP4."
                     /protein_id="NP_740471.1"
     proprotein      3386..5110
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="precursor polypeptide P2"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:Amino acid sequence analysis and
                     were found to be proteolytic cleavage products of the
                     polyprotein.[6264310]"
                     /note="P2 precursor polypeptide is a precursor of
                     nonstructural proteins, which is released from the
                     polypeptide chain by proteolytic processing mediated by
                     virally-encoded proteinases 2A pro to ultimately 3 mature
                     viral proteins: 2A, 2B and 2C. P2 proteins are primarily
                     responsible for the biochemical and structural changes that
                     occur in the infected cell."
     mat_peptide     3386..3832
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="protease 2A"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:protein expression[3011278]"
                     /note="Picornain 2A (Protein 2A) is a small
                     chymotrypsin-like cysteine proteinase. It is responsible
                     for the cleavage between the P1 and P2 regions. In order to
                     shut down the capped cellular mRNA transcription, picornain
                     2A cleaves the host translation initiation factor EIF4G1
                     and induces apoptotic cell death."
                     /protein_id="NP_740477.1"
     proprotein      3833..5110
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="protein 2BC"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:protein expression[3011278]"
                     /note="Processing of 2BC by 3Cpro gives rise to the mature
                     products 2B and 2C, although a large fraction of 2BC
                     remains uncleaved in picornavirus-infected cells. The
                     expression of poliovirus 2BC protein in yeast and mammalian
                     cells leads to a number of metabolic and morphological
                     alterations, such as growth inhibition, intracellular
                     membrane proliferation, blockade of the exocytic pathway,
                     and enhanced membrane permeability."
     mat_peptide     3833..4123
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="protein 2B"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:protein expression[3011278]"
                     /note="Protein 2B enhances membrane permeability."
                     /protein_id="NP_740472.1"
     mat_peptide     4124..5110
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="protein 2C"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:protein expression[3011278]"
                     /note="Involved in initiation and elongation of RNA
                     synthesis, RNA encapsidation, virus uncoating and guanidine
                     resistance (Asn179-Gly mutation). Putative helicase III.~2C
                     protein (together with 2BC protein) induces the formation
                     of host cell endoplasmic reticulum-derived rosette-like
                     membranous structures, located in the cytoplasm, where the
                     process of viral RNA replication takes place."
                     /protein_id="NP_740473.1"
     proprotein      5111..7369
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="precursor polypeptide P3"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:Amino acid sequence analysis
                     cleavage products of the polyprotein.[6264310]"
                     /note="Processing of the P3 precursor occurs by two
                     independent pathways, major and minor. In the major
                     pathway, processing between 3B and 3C yields 3AB and 3CD.
                     In the minor pathway, processing between 3A and 3B yields
                     3A and 3BCD. 3BCD processing yields 3BC and 3D; 3BC
                     processing yields 3B and 3C."
     mat_peptide     5111..5437
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="protein 3AB"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:Poliovirus polyprotein processing by
                     the Gly-Gly mutant evaluated by Western blotting.
                     [18779320]"
                     /note="Poliovirus protein 3AB displayes nucleic acid
                     chaperone activity in promoting the hybridization of
                     complementary nucleic acids and destabilizing secondary
                     structure. It also stimulates the rate of binding between
                     complementary nucleic acid, demonstrates
                     helix-destabilizing activity, and serves as a donor for VPg
                     uridylylation."
                     /protein_id="YP_007353733.1"
     mat_peptide     5111..5371
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="protein 3A"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:Poliovirus polyprotein processing by
                     the Gly-Gly mutant evaluated by Western blotting.
                     [18779320]"
                     /note="Poliovirus protein 3A is a small, membrane-binding
                     protein that plays multiple roles in viral RNA replication
                     complex formation and function. In the infected cell, this
                     protein associates with other viral and cellular proteins
                     as part of a supramolecular complex."
                     /protein_id="NP_740474.1"
     proprotein      5372..7369
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="precursor protein 3BCD"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:Poliovirus polyprotein processing by
                     the Gly-Gly mutant evaluated by Western
                     blotting.[18779320]"
                     /note="3BCD precursor protein is a precursor of 3BC and 3D
                     proteins. Uncleaved precursor 3BCD is one of the substrates
                     for uridylylation of VPg protein."
     mat_peptide     5372..5437
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="viral protein genome-linked"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:Poliovirus polyprotein processing by
                     the Gly-Gly mutant evaluated by Western blotting.
                     [18779320]"
                     /note="VPg (3B), a small protein that binds viral RNA and
                     is necessary for synthesis of viral positive and negative
                     strand RNA."
                     /protein_id="NP_740475.1"
     mat_peptide     5438..7369
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="protein 3CD"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:Poliovirus polyprotein processing by
                     the Gly-Gly mutant evaluated by Western blotting.
                     [18779320]"
                     /note="3CD protein lacks polymerase activity, but possesses
                     protease activity with substrate recognition properties
                     distinct from those of 3C protein. It was shown that
                     cleavage of the viral capsid proteins, located in the
                     N-terminal portion of the poliovirus polyprotein, requires
                     3CD-catalyzed proteolysis. 3CD protease activity has been
                     implicated in cleavage of several host proteins. In
                     addition to its proteolytic activities, 3CD also involved
                     in viral RNA replication process. The protein binds to the
                     cloverleaf structure at the 5? terminus of poliovirus RNA,
                     and this binding was shown to be important for virus
                     replication. 3CD also stimulates uridylylation of viral
                     protein VPg, catalyzed by 3D, which is required for
                     initiation of RNA replication, by binding to the template
                     for uridylylation on the cis-acting replication element.
                     3CD protein interacts with the cellular heterogeneous
                     nuclear ribonucleoprotein (hnRNP) C1/C2, which forms a
                     specific RNP complex with the poliovirus 3? nontranslated
                     region that is thought to be important for replication. 3CD
                     (as well as another poliovirus protein, 3A), induces the
                     recruitment to membranes of cellular proteins from the
                     family of small GTPases, designated Arfs (ADP ribosylation
                     factors)."
                     /protein_id="YP_007353734.1"
     mat_peptide     5438..5986
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="protease 3C"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:Poliovirus polyprotein processing by
                     the Gly-Gly mutant evaluated by Western
                     blotting.[18779320]"
                     /note="Chymotrypsin-like cystein proteinase 3C. Viral 3C
                     protease (3Cpro) plays a major role in translation
                     regulation. It cleaves poly(A)-binding protein (PABP) and
                     removes the C-terminal domain (CTD) that interacts with
                     several translation factors. 3C protein has been shown to
                     function as a stimulatory factor for 3Dpol in the VPg
                     uridylylation reaction."
                     /protein_id="NP_740476.2"
     mat_peptide     5987..7369
                     /locus_tag="PVgp1"
                     /product="RNA-directed RNA polymerase"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:Poliovirus polyprotein processing by
                     the Gly-Gly mutant evaluated by Western blotting.
                     [18779320]"
                     /note="3D; The RNA-dependent RNA-polymerase, 3Dpol, is an
                     essential component in genome for the replication of single
                     stranded RNA. 3Dpol catalyze two independend half-reactions
                     leading to the attachment of VPg protein to the 5' end of
                     viral RNA. First, VPg is uridylylated to produce VPg-pUpU;
                     second, VPg-pUpU serves as a primer for full-length RNA
                     synthesis"
                     /protein_id="NP_740478.2"
