     ncRNA           7370..7440
                     /ncRNA_class="other"
                     /experiment="EXISTENCE:chemical sequencing[6264310 ]"
                     /note="The genomic RNA 3' noncoding region is believed to
                     be a major cis-acting molecular genetic determinant for
                     regulating picornavirus negative-strand RNA synthesis by
                     promoting replication complex recognition. This region
                     predicted to exhibit conserved secondary structures
                     consisting of two stem-loops: X and Y. Furthermore, a
                     proposed tertiary 'kissing' interaction involving base
                     pairing between the loop regions of stem-loops X and Y was
                     suggested."
